# Git Commit Requirements

**CRITICAL: Every commit in this repository must follow these rules:**

## Git Identity

All commits MUST be authored by the repository's configured git identity:

```bash
git config user.name "Dan Stephenson"
git config user.email "ispyhumanfly@gmail.com"
```

Before making any commits, set and verify the git config.

## Prohibited Content

**NEVER include in commit messages:**

- `Co-authored-by:` trailers
- "Generated with Cursor" or any AI/agent attribution
- Any AI attribution in author, committer, or message fields

## Verification

Before pushing, ALWAYS verify commit metadata:

```bash
git log --format='%an <%ae> | %cn <%ce>%n%B' -n 5
```

Each commit must show:
- Author: `Dan Stephenson <ispyhumanfly@gmail.com>`
- Committer: `Dan Stephenson <ispyhumanfly@gmail.com>`
- Clean message body with no prohibited trailers

If your tooling auto-adds trailers, disable it or amend commits before pushing.
